From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:47:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: show a poll's votes in the Messaging app, and a
 received mention in bold

* Show a poll's votes in the Messaging app, and log a vote

A Telegram poll reached the app without counts, so votes made
elsewhere never showed. The app draws them from the poll token's
"votes", one count for each option in the options' order, as
purple-combined gives them for WhatsApp, rewriting the poll message
in place, which the app takes for no edit by the sender.

webos::pollToken takes the counts. A poll is shown with them, each
option's voter_count, where TDLib lets us see them (poll.
can_see_results): until we have voted, or unless the poll is closed or
ours, TDLib 1.8.67 gives every count as 0 and can_see_results as false
(PollManager::get_poll_object), and a 0 that is no count is not shown.
"max" and the options stay as they were.

A user's client hears of a change to a poll as updateMessageContent for
each message carrying it (PollManager::notify_on_poll_update);
updatePoll is for bots only (td_api.tl). Either way the poll is given
again as a whole with "webos-im-edit" (account, serviceMessageId, text),
the line of a forward kept in front of it as it was shown, and only
where the text has changed: a pending answer, say, changes nothing the
app shows. TdAccountData keeps, for each poll message shown, TDLib's id
of the poll and the text given, so updatePoll finds the messages too.
That a poll was closed is now told this way too, with its final counts,
rather than as an edit notice followed by the poll once more. A poll
still waiting to be shown takes the new content, to be shown as it is
by then.

Our own choice (pollOption.is_chosen) is not given: the app reads it
from the message's myPollVote, which only the app writes, and the
token has no place for it.

The vote from the app ("webos-im-send-poll-vote", void, so every
plug-in sees it and the protocol check picks ours) left no trace when
it went well, nor did sendQuery say what it sent. It now logs that a
vote was asked for which message, how many of the poll's options are
voted for, and that TDLib took it, without the options' text.

Unit tests in test/webos-commands-test.cpp and
test/webos-receive-test.cpp.

* Show a received mention in bold

A Telegram message that names someone, by username ("@name") or by
name with a link to them (textEntityTypeMention and
textEntityTypeMentionName in td_api.tl), reached the Messaging app as
plain text. Show it in bold, as purple-presage does for Signal, so
mentions look the same on every service: getEntityMarkup gives both
entity types <b>..</b>, so getMessageText marks them up as it does
bold, nested with any other formatting. Offsets count UTF-16 code
units, as before. Nothing is added to a mention by name, which shows
the name as written, and a text to be sent keeps a mention plain.

The quote a reply carries is left plain: the app shows it as text, and
it is filled from the message's plain text.

This is for the Messaging app only (isWebosUi()): other front-ends show
a mention plain, as before.

Unit tests in test/webos-mention-test.cpp and
test/webos-commands-test.cpp.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
